__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
venv/
.git
.gitignore
*.sqlite3
media/
staticfiles/
*.md
# ...except the changelog, which the app reads at runtime to fill the sidebar
# "What's new" dialog. The `*.md` line above dropped it from the image, and
# because a missing changelog is rendered as an empty dialog rather than an
# error, production simply had no release notes at all. Keep the negation
# *after* `*.md` -- Docker applies patterns in order and the last match wins.
!CHANGELOG.md
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
